implementationPlan.description:
Read the landed prerequisites FIRST and adapt names. VSC-15 can be claimed only once VSC-14 (task-720f81a6) is DONE, and with it VSC-13 (task-065e4812) and VSC-12 (task-daf5abdd).
This plan assumes the following, posted in #architects as msg-a53702b5. Where the landed code differs, use the landed names; the BEHAVIOUR below is the contract.
- VSC-12 client: addAccount(label?), removeAccount(accountId), moveAccount(accountId, -1|1), renameAccount(accountId, label) and setAccountSwitchPercent(percent), each returning boolean (false = not connected). Also an accountRotation getter, onAccountsChanged, and onAccountAdded (the new account id from ACCOUNT_ADDED).
- Existing client members: connectionState and onConnectionChanged.
- VSC-13: moe-vscode/src/util/AccountPresentation.ts exports parseAccountRotation(unknown), actions(rotation, selectedId, connected), isValidLabel and resolveAccountText.
- VSC-14: moe-vscode/src/providers/AccountsTreeProvider.ts, with account elements that carry the account id, a require map in tests/accounts-view.test.cjs, and registrations in extension.ts.
Then write moe-vscode/tests/accounts-actions.test.cjs with the Write tool.
- Harness: load the provider under node:vm with VSC-14's require map (the real AccountPresentation.ts transpiled and loaded with a throwing require, plus a fake vscode), and put Buffer and console in the context.
- Fake vscode: recorders for window.showInputBox (queued answers), showWarningMessage (queued answers), showInformationMessage, showErrorMessage, createTerminal (a fake terminal recording sendText and show), commands.registerCommand (id to callback), commands.executeCommand (records setContext) and env.clipboard.writeText, plus whatever VSC-14's provider already uses (EventEmitter, TreeItem, ...).
- Fake client: recorder senders with per-test return values, and EventEmitters.
- Compare vm-realm values through JSON or field by field (mem:gotcha-vscode-vm-test-harness).
Its error handling: an unreadable corpus, bundle or package.json fails naming the path, and the per-row corpus checks report every failing id at once.
Tests:
1. package.json and registration:
   - contributes.commands declares moe.accounts.add, .signIn, .remove, .moveUp, .moveDown, .rename and .setSwitchPercent. The titles of the first six equal the bundle's moe.accounts.button.add/signIn/remove/moveUp/moveDown/rename;
   - menus view/title holds add and setSwitchPercent with `view == moe.accounts && moe.accounts.canAdd` / `... && moe.accounts.canSwitchAt`;
   - menus view/item/context holds the other five with `view == moe.accounts && viewItem =~ /\bcanX\b/` (canSignIn, canRemove, canMoveUp, canMoveDown, canRename);
   - provider.registerCommands() registers exactly those seven ids.
2. Context keys over every rotation row of moe-jetbrains/src/test/resources/client-accounts.json:
   - set the fake client's accountRotation and connection state from the row and refresh;
   - the last setContext values of moe.accounts.canAdd and moe.accounts.canSwitchAt equal expectActions.add and .switchAt;
   - the element whose id is row.selectedId has contextValue tokens equal to {canRename: rename, canMoveUp: moveUp, canMoveDown: moveDown, canRemove: removeOnly || signOutAndRemove, canSignIn: signIn} from expectActions;
   - every element's tokens equal the same mapping of AccountPresentation.actions for its own id.
3. Actions, each through the registered callback with an element:
   - add: 'Work Max' sends addAccount('Work Max') once; a cancel or a 65-char label sends nothing; onAccountAdded('acct-new') after a sent add opens exactly one terminal running `login acct-new`, and without a pending add it opens none;
   - signIn opens one terminal with `login <id>`;
   - remove: 'Remove only' sends removeAccount(id) once; 'Sign out and remove' runs `remove <id> --sign-out` in a terminal and sends nothing; a dismiss does nothing;
   - moveUp and moveDown send moveAccount(id, -1) and moveAccount(id, 1);
   - rename sends renameAccount(id, label) for a new label, and nothing for a cancel, an invalid label or the unchanged label;
   - switch percent: '75' sends setAccountSwitchPercent(75); a cancel, the current value, '0', '101', '7.5' and 'x' send nothing;
   - every sender returning false shows exactly 'Not connected to Moe daemon \u2014 the account change was not sent.'
4. Quoting, through the exported accountsCommandLine with node '/opt/my node/node', script "/opt/moe's/cli.js", registryFile 'C:\\Users\\A B\\claude accounts.json' and id 'acct-"q" 1':
   - bash: every word is single-quoted with the '\\'' idiom;
   - windows: base64-decode (utf16le) the -EncodedCommand and find `& '...'` with single quotes doubled;
   - a CR, LF or NUL in any word throws, and the signIn handler then shows an error and opens no terminal.
5. Strings: every dialog text equals its MoeBundle.properties value, read as UTF-8 with `\n` decoded and args substituted. That covers add.title/prompt, rename.title/prompt, remove.confirm ({0} = label), remove.signOut, remove.only, terminal.tab and terminal.unavailable.

Adversarial self-review of this task's diff, the only review step.
- Would a test fail if:
  - add skipped isValidLabel;
  - onAccountAdded signed in an account nobody added here;
  - remove sent on dismiss;
  - rename sent an unchanged label;
  - the switch percent accepted 7.5;
  - a stale menu bypassed the fresh actions check;
  - quoting used double quotes;
  - a CR in an id reached the terminal;
  - setContext ran before registerCommands?
- Is every user-visible string either bundle-equal or pinned by the test?
- Any value import added to the provider?
- Confirm with `git status --porcelain` that the task touched only moe-vscode/package.json, moe-vscode/src/providers/AccountsTreeProvider.ts (edited, not recreated), moe-vscode/src/extension.ts and moe-vscode/tests/accounts-actions.test.cjs, plus accounts-view.test.cjs only if step 4's fallback was unavoidable, and named.
- Peers own every other dirty path: never revert, stage or commit them.
- Report every touched file in complete_step.modifiedFiles.
